<title>SINGAPORE: ABR Holdings 1996 net falls 57.5 percent.</title>
<headline>ABR Holdings 1996 net falls 57.5 percent.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				0.30 vs  0.70</p>
<p>    Dividend (percent)		    3.00 vs  3.00</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		     0.70 vs  1.60</p>
<p>    Turnover				 29.83 vs 30.69</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	 0.45 vs  0.57</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		    0.09 vs  0.06</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation	   1.58 vs  1.52</p>
<p>    Profits from associates	     0.53 vs  0.21</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			  1.26 vs  0.35</p>
<p>    Tax					 0.49 vs  0.71</p>
<p>    Minorities  (gains)		   0.05 vs  1.27</p>
<p>    Dividend pay date:		    July 18, 1997</p>
<p>    Last day books open:		  June 30, 1997</p>
<p>Note - ABR Holdings Ltd is a food and beverage company.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
